## 1. Context — what we are computing and why the lift+IBP combination is needed

Reproducing the 4-point loop-seed `J^00(r1,r2)` of arXiv:2211.03810 `fig_trispectrum`
(`CROSSCHECK/fourpt/`), principal series `μ = i ν̃` (⇒ **complex** monomial/polynomial exponents),
single-squeezed slice `r2=0.9`, `r1 ∈ [1e-4, 1e-0.5]`. Two facts force the lift × IBP combination:

1. **Divergence.** `J^00` has a single simple UV pole (`[…]_MS̄` in eq. 12). In the repo
   decomposition the divergent cones live only in `++` presectors 1–2, **one divergent variable per
   cone, `c_k = 2/7`** (see `Fourptpp/.../RESULTS/divergence_map_fourpt.m`). So per physics there is
   **exactly one simple pole and no nested/higher-order divergence.**
2. **Hierarchy.** At deep squeeze `k12 = 1/r1 → 1e4`, the master polynomial coefficient `4·k12`
   spans ~10^4. This is exactly the regime the auxiliary-variable uplift targets; without it the
   tropical map mismatches the integrand and Vegas variance blows up.

We need **IBP** (per the off-axis pole structure; Subtraction/pinned-ε cannot resolve `θ≠0`, see
`planIBPCX §1.2`) **combined with the uplift** (for the hierarchy), on the divergent presectors.

