## 5. The feature (assuming case A; the common, expected case)

Make the IBP **divergence classification** off-axis-aware everywhere it counts directions, mirroring
what `ibpImagPole`/the driver branch already do for the prefactor:

1. **`IBPReduceSector` divergent-variable detection** (`Re(α0)≤0` test, ~`:4832`, `:4988`) and the
   **`nDiv`/`nestedIBP` gate** (`:4986–4992`, `:5010–5013`): a direction counts as a *pole* only when
   `Re(α0)=0` **and** `PossibleZeroQ[ibpImagPole-style θ for that direction] == True`. Off-axis
   directions (`Re=0, Im≠0`) are excluded from `nDiv`.
2. **Post-IBP `verify all α0>0`** (`:5148–5157`): pass a direction with `Re(α0)=0` **iff** its
   imaginary part is nonzero (off-axis ⇒ finite ⇒ OK); only fail on a true `Re≤0 ∧ Im=0` residual.
3. **Reduce off-axis directions to finite, not pole.** Each off-axis direction gets one IBP step
   (raising its exponent so `|y^{Re}| ` is bounded — `planIBPCX §1.2`); its contribution is the finite
   `1/(iθ)` boundary+bulk (the `:6240–6241` off-axis branch), **not** a `1/ε` residue. Multiple off-axis
   directions ⇒ multiple finite IBP steps; still **one** `1/ε` pole (the `Im=0` direction) per sector.

Exactness/byte-identity (per `planIBPCX §6`): the new branch activates only when some `Re=0`
direction has `Im≠0`; the real/θ=0 path is untouched (`cc_45/46/47/48` and the IBP codegen goldens
stay green).

If case (B): the above is still necessary but not sufficient — `nestedIBP` must additionally allow a
genuine second IBP reduction (iterated IBP) for the per-cone higher-order residual.

